## Summary

The bug was in `packages/babel-generator/src/source-map.ts`, in the `SourceMap.mark()` method.

**Root cause:** When Babel transforms code that already carries an external input source map (e.g. a bundle), each output position is looked up against the input map via `originalPositionFor` to chain back to the true pre-bundle source. The input map records both the original *position* and the original *name* for that position. The old code used the input map's name only as a guard — it took the source *position* from the input map but attached the name derived from the **current AST identifier** (`loc.identifierName || node.name`). When a plugin renamed a variable (e.g. an inner `root` → `root2$$$`/`_root$$$` to avoid colliding with an outer `root$$$`), the emitted name was the renamed/bundle-local name instead of the authoritative original name from the input map.

**Fix:** When an input source map is present and its lookup yields a name for the position, that name is now used as the authoritative original name; the AST-derived `identifierName` and the `identifierNamePos` fallback are only used when the input map has no name:

```ts
if (originalMapping.name) {
  identifierName = originalMapping.name;
} else if (identifierNamePos) {
  const originalIdentifierMapping = originalPositionFor(this._inputMap, identifierNamePos);
  if (originalIdentifierMapping.name) {
    identifierName = originalIdentifierMapping.name;
  }
}
```

This makes the output map's names, mappings, and preserved fields (`sources`, `sourcesContent`, `version`, `ignoreList`) all chain faithfully back through the input source map.

